# CODEOWNERS — human review gate for compliance-sensitive content
# =================================================================
#
# Purpose: the autonomous Learn Monitor documentation pipeline (Stage 1) lets an
# agent DRAFT documentation edits, but a human must approve any change to
# customer-facing compliance content before it merges. This file names the
# required reviewer(s) for those paths.
#
# IMPORTANT — this file is necessary but NOT sufficient on its own. For it to
# act as an enforced merge gate, branch protection on `main` must be configured
# (by a repo admin) to **"Require review from Code Owners"**. Without that
# setting, CODEOWNERS only requests review; it does not block merge. As of this
# commit, `main` branch protection requires 11 status checks but NOT a code-owner
# review — enabling that is a tracked Stage 1 prerequisite.
#
# Syntax: <path-pattern>  <owner ...>   (last matching pattern wins)
#
# NOTE: there is deliberately NO catch-all (`* @owner`) rule. A catch-all would
# require code-owner review on *every* PR (including tooling) and would deadlock
# the maintainer's own PRs (GitHub forbids self-approval). Only the explicit
# compliance-sensitive paths below require code-owner review. With a single
# maintainer, "Require review from Code Owners" is intended primarily to gate
# *bot-authored* autodoc PRs (which the maintainer reviews); the maintainer's own
# edits to these paths would need a second reviewer if that rule is enabled.

# --- Customer-facing compliance content (always human-reviewed) ---
/docs/controls/                     @judeper
/docs/reference/                    @judeper
/docs/framework/                    @judeper
/docs/playbooks/                    @judeper
/mkdocs.yml                         @judeper

# Machine-readable control manifest (drives the assessment engine + scoring).
/assessment/manifest/controls.json  @judeper

# --- Autonomous-pipeline safety machinery (privileged; review with care) ---
# The routing gate, canary, and (future) cross-vendor verifier ARE the controls
# that decide what may be auto-handled, so changes to them are high-trust.
/scripts/autodoc_*.py               @judeper
/.github/workflows/                 @judeper
/.github/CODEOWNERS                 @judeper

# --- Trusted dependency-artifact gate (base-controlled; highest trust) ---
# These paths are the authoritative supply-chain policy. They are read only from
# the protected default branch, and the gate fails closed when a pull request
# changes any of them alongside a guarded dependency path. Changing an expected
# pin, an allowlist, or the gate itself is a deliberate, separately reviewed act.
# See .github/TRUSTED-DEPENDENCY-GATE.md.
/.github/trusted-policy/            @judeper
/.github/branch-protection.json     @judeper
/scripts/trusted/                   @judeper

# Reviewed dependency artifacts and the verifiers that bind them.
/scripts/verify-*.mjs               @judeper
/vendor/                            @judeper
